This repair package does not redistribute the PPero sequence archive or source
code. It includes an independently implemented repair to the user-supplied
bi-profile evaluation code. Original input files must be acquired with their
provenance recorded before analysis. Preserve upstream notices when adding data.
The MIT licence applies to original code, not to third-party data or manuscripts.

Changes to the user-supplied code
Supervised profiles are fitted inside each tuning and calibration training split.
Group boundaries are respected at each split. Invalid residues and short sequences
are rejected instead of silently deleted or padded. Synthetic regression tests
are separated from scientific validation. No manuscript results are claimed from
these code tests. Scientific evaluation of this repair has not been run.

PPero's training sequences cannot serve as an independent test set for PPero.
This package does not claim a head-to-head comparison with PPero.
